---
/**
 * MathStyles — the conditional KaTeX stylesheet link (risk #12).
 *
 * Rendered into <head> via the layout's `head` slot ONLY when frontmatter says
 * `math: true`, so pages with no equations pay nothing. The file it points at
 * is vendored out of the npm package by scripts/sync-katex-assets.mjs — never a
 * CDN (§2.4).
 *
 * The two <link rel="preload"> hints cover the faces every equation on this
 * site actually uses: KaTeX_Main-Regular for upright text and digits, and
 * KaTeX_Math-Italic for variables. Without them the browser cannot discover a
 * font until it has parsed the stylesheet and laid out the equation, which
 * shows a frame of fallback glyphs at the wrong metrics. Preloading ALL twenty
 * faces would be worse than none, so this is deliberately the short list; a
 * page using \mathcal or \mathfrak simply loads those two the normal way.
 */
---

<link
  rel="preload"
  as="font"
  type="font/woff2"
  href="/katex/fonts/KaTeX_Main-Regular.woff2"
  crossorigin
/>
<link
  rel="preload"
  as="font"
  type="font/woff2"
  href="/katex/fonts/KaTeX_Math-Italic.woff2"
  crossorigin
/>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/katex/katex.min.css" />
